 For a subscription, tokens describe allowance use; incremental cash cost is
 unknown. The provisional lowest-token option is a starting point, not a
 quality-gated recommendation.
+
+Plans may add hard provider and data-region policies under `restrictions`, for
+example `provider: { "allowed": ["OpenAI"], "source": "organization policy" }`
+and `data_region: { "allowed": ["eu-west"], "source": "residency policy" }`.
+Each candidate can report `provider_evidence` and `data_region_evidence` as
+`{ "value": "...", "source": "..." }`. When either configured policy has no
+candidate evidence, that policy and the candidate stand unknown, and
+`development run` refuses the candidate. The source labels identify the policy
+and evidence used in the comparison; they do not establish facts beyond those
+sources.
